──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
Third-party components vendored or referenced
──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────

Following the zero-dependency C99 architectural consolidation:
  * OpenSSL: Purged. Cryptographic primitives migrated to in-tree determ::c99.
  * Asio 1.30.2: Purged. Replaced with native zero-dependency POSIX/kqueue/epoll sockets (<sys/socket.h>).
  * nlohmann/json: Purged. Consensus networking relies strictly on canonical Big-Endian binary wire format; RPC utilizes in-place, zero-allocation C99 token parsing.

All core consensus, networking, and cryptographic primitives execute
under bare-metal C99 with zero dynamic third-party library dependencies.

